# internal working files of the routine that produced this repo — not published
challenge-brief.md
seed-design.md
challenge-page-*.html
challenge-submit-*.html
# the submission receipt and packet carry the operator's email address (flagged by
# scripts/screen_tree.py). They are evidence for the routine, never for the public repo:
# without these lines a `git add -A` would publish a personal address.
submission-receipt-*
submission-packet.md

# the AgentHarm PROMPT TEXTS, fetched by scripts/eval_agent_loop.py into a local cache.
# tests/corpus/FETCH.md promises this repository does not redistribute the harm corpus:
# 208 harmful prompts written to drive an agent into harmful tool use. Only ids,
# decisions and counts are checked in (tests/agent-loop-eval.json), so the published
# numbers stay re-derivable without republishing the corpus. Without this line a
# `git add -A` in the publishing clone would push the whole harmful split.
tests/cache/
